        "answer": {
          "short": "$y = x - 3$",
          "worked": "Read points from the graph in increasing $x$ order and enter them in a table: $(-1,-4), (0,-3), (1,-2), (2,-1)$.\n\nFor an increase of $1$ in $x$, $y$ changes by $1$. Thus $m=1$. The table gives $y=-3$ when $x=0$, so $c=-3$.\n\n$y = x - 3$. Check by substituting another plotted point: $x=2$ gives $y=-1$.",
